  "instructions": "When the user asks to connect Garmin, call connect_garmin. It prepares Chrome and starts browser sign-in in a background helper. The user enters passwords and MFA directly on Garmin's website. Call check_garmin_auth for completion; do not repeatedly start login while pending. No sample workout is needed during setup. NETWORK_ERROR, RATE_LIMITED and GARMIN_UNAVAILABLE do not require signing in again. Never automatically retry a workout write after an uncertain network failure; inspect the account first. For training shorthand, WU/CD means warm-up/cool-down, T means threshold/tempo, and R/r means recovery. Use lapButton duration when the user requests variable time; do not invent numerical effort targets. Updates replace the whole workout, so fetch before updating. Naming by date does not request calendar scheduling.",
